 ### Magic3D
-A method targeting issues caused by low-resolution diffusion images using a two-stage coarse-fine approach [S3]. In the coarse stage, Magic3D uses Instant-NGP as the NeRF model trained from images generated from text prompts using the image diffusion model eDiff-I [S3]. In the fine stage, the coarse geometry extracted from Instant-NGP is placed on a mesh, which is optimized over in the fine stage using images generated with a latent diffusion model [S3]. Experiments over 397 prompts generated objects, each rated by three users, showed a preference toward Magic3D over DreamFusion [S3].
+A method targeting issues caused by low-resolution diffusion images using a two-stage coarse-fine approach [S4]. In the coarse stage, Magic3D uses Instant-NGP as the NeRF model trained from images generated from text prompts using the image diffusion model eDiff-I [S4]. In the fine stage, the coarse geometry extracted from Instant-NGP is placed on a mesh, which is optimized over in the fine stage using images generated with a latent diffusion model [S4]. Experiments over 397 prompts generated objects, each rated by three users, showed a preference toward Magic3D over DreamFusion [S4].
 
